  {
    "@id": "https://ticketpro.ca/event/1694540788",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2026-09-10T19:30:00-06:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "https://ticketpro.ca/place/1100063650"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tprowest.ticketpro.ca/api/v1/resources/1694494609.jpeg?version=2"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/offers": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tprowest.ticketpro.ca/genid/29a54ff71b658481"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tprowest.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/Maclab_StevePoltz/performances/MAC10IS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tprowest.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/Maclab_StevePoltz/performances/MAC10IS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Steve Poltz - Maclab Performance Series"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p><b></b></p>\n\n<p>A dude named Steve Poltz (me) in East Nashville wakes up one morning and gets a call from another dude in East Nashville named Dex Green. Dex says, 'Hey man, you live so close. You oughta come over and make some music. Maybe we'll document it — who knows, maybe it's a record.'</p>\n\n<p>Capturing me in a studio is like convincing a whirling dervish to stop spinning long enough to sign a bill into law. It's chaos, caffeine, and accidental poetry — art colliding with microphones and commerce in a glorious mess. That's how JoyRide happened. No seatbelts, no helmets. Just unsaturated, unadulterated art. Real humans making real noise in real time.</p>\n\n<p>JoyRide is my 14th solo album (not counting the Rugburns records, live things, and bootlegs floating around). I tour nonstop, so I usually have to be tricked into a studio under the guise of 'just one song.'</p>\n\n<p>According to Wikipedia, Steve Poltz (me) is a Canadian-American singer-songwriter and guitarist. He is a founding member of the indie-rock band the Rugburns and collaborated on several songs with singer Jewel, including the 1996 single 'You Were Meant for Me', which reached number 2 in the US.</p>\n\n<p><b><a href='https://poltz.com/' target='_blank'>poltz.com</a></b></p>\n\n<iframe width='560' height='315' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/R4qmqgjj4Do?si=J6bQbkUhai5QKljY' title='YouTube video player' frameborder='0' allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe>\n\n<p><b><big>Subscriptions on sale now: <a href='https://tpromaclab.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/Maclab_2627' target='_blank'>CLICK HERE TO PURCHASE</a></big></b></p> \n<style>\n.location-page-temp {\n    display: block!important;}\n@media screen and (max-width: 600px){iframe{width:100%;}}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
