        "@id": "https://ticketpro.ca/place/8681939"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tprowest.ticketpro.ca/api/v1/resources/1696980803.jpeg?version=1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/offers": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tprowest.ticketpro.ca/genid/4464fdc2280828cc"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://tprowest.ticketpro.ca/genid/eb6a2266d5978f2b"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tprowest.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1696980903/performances/MAJ19IS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tprowest.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1696980903/performances/MAJ19IS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Keith Alessi: Tomatoes Tried to Kill Me But Banjos Saved My Life"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p>Tomatoes Tried to Kill Me But Banjos Saved My Life isn't just a show, it's a cause. A heartfelt passion project that began as a nudge after Keith Alessi's life took a major turn, it has been his mission to raise money for causes close to his heart. Through donations, including 100% of all artist fees, the show has raised over $1.2 Million Dollars (CAD) as of December 2025 for various charities including cancer organizations, music programs, community groups and artist funding and development.   </p>\n\n<p>The show has sold out runs across Canada, Off-Broadway in New York City, and at the Edinburgh Fringe Festival in Scotland 3 years in a row. It has toured internationally, including Canada, the US, England, Scotland and Australia. Keith shares his exceptional true story of leaving the world of corporate board rooms behind to follow his long-delayed passion-playing the banjo! When faced with a deadly cancer battle, his musical pursuit took him on a journey that became the key to saving his life. Told through authentic storytelling, heartfelt humor and music, Keith's story is an uplifting tale of challenge, triumph, and the the healing power of the arts and music.</p>\n\n<p>Biggar & District Arts Council, Castwell & Company Performing Arts, and New Creation Community Players are pleased to present Keith Alessi's 'Tomatoes Tried to Kill Me But Banjos Saved My Life' with proceeds going to Farm In The Dell Biggar.</p>\n\n<iframe width='560' height='315' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/_E5-Xo1LyfU?si=5LALKEbMZ1tJyfDy' title='YouTube video player' frameborder='0' allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe>\n\n<style>\n.location-page-temp {display: block!important;}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
