      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "National Day for Truth & Reconciliation"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "\n<p>Join us for an evening of reflection and connection as we\nmark the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation. This\ngathering creates space to journey through the truths of\nCanada's past, deepen our understanding of the present,\nand envision a future rooted in respect, justice, and shared\nresponsibility.</p>\n\nThrough stories, reflections, and open conversation, we will\nhonour the lived experiences of Indigenous Peoples and\nconfront the ongoing impacts of colonialism. This is a time\nto listen, learn, and explore how each of us can commit\nto the work of healing and reconciliation. Participants will\nhave the opportunity to ask questions, either in real time\nor anonymously. All are welcome. To close the evening, tea,\nbannock, and light refreshments will be served. Emotional\nsupport will be available throughout the event. </p>\n\n\n"
      }
    ],
