    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Murder For Two - Royal Canadian Theatre Company"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p>Presented by Royal Canadian Theatre Company</p>\n\n<p>Book by Kellen Blair and Joe Kinosian<br>\nLyrics by Kellen Blair<br>\nMusic by Joe Kinosian</p>\n\n<p>Murder for Two is the story of a disastrous surprise birthday party for novelist Arthur Whitney. The big surprise was that one of the guests murdered the novelist because he had the habit of revealing his friends darkest, naughtiest secrets in his novels. First on the scene is small town cop Marcus Moscowicz, who has dreams of becoming a big city detective, and solving this case in record time could be his ticket to the big time. There are 13 suspects and they all have good reason to want Whitney dead and buried, so Moscowicz has his job cut out for him.</p>\n\n<style>\n.location-page-temp {display: block!important;}\n@media screen and (max-width: 600px){iframe{width:100%;}}\n</style>\n"
      }
    ],
