    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "I Don't Belong Here - Songs & Stories Remembered"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "\n<p><b><font color='#ff0000'>Contains Mature Themes and Language</font></b></p>\n\n<p>Written by and featuring Joëlle Rabu and Kelly Wyatt,\nI Don't Belong Here - Stories and Songs Remembered\nis a poignant and deeply human stage production\nexploring life inside a dementia care facility. Directed\nby Kymme Patrick with music direction by Nico\nRhodes, the production unfolds through a series of\nvignettes portraying residents, family members, and\ncompassionate caregivers navigating memory, loss,\nhumour, and connection.</p>\n<p>Balancing emotional depth with moments of warmth and\nlevity, this intimate three-person ensemble piece offers a\nmoving meditation on love, dignity, and resilience. The music\nof Harry Nilsson provides a haunting and beautiful backdrop,\nwith songs that transcend generations and resonate\ndeeply with the fragility and wonder of everyday life. </p>\n\n<p><a href='https://joellerabu.com/' target='_blank'>joellerabu.com</a></p>\n\n<p><i>This show is supported by the City\nof Spruce Grove, Parkland County,\nthe Town of Stony Plain and\nWestView Dementia Collaborative</i></p>\n\n"
      }
    ],
